    [KV Pool][BugFix] Remove MemCache DP initialization barrier (#19370)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Revert #17289 because the MemCache DP initialization barrier is no
    longer needed. Remove the CPU process-group barrier after MemCache store
    initialization, its configuration propagation through
    `AscendStoreConnector` and `KVPoolWorker`, and the barrier-specific
    tests. Clean up the deployment guide, GLM5.3-Flash examples, and Chinese
    translations that reference the removed option. Document that the
    MemCache pooling backend requires both `memcache-hybrid >= 1.3.0` and
    `memfabric-hybrid >= 1.3.0`, including version constraints in the
    installation commands and matching Chinese translations.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. MemCache initialization no longer waits for a DP process-group
    barrier. The `kv_connector_extra_config.memcache_dp_init_barrier` option
    is removed and should be removed from deployment configurations.
    
    Release note: `release_notes/fragments/19370.yaml`.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Single signed-off commit based on main
    `041cfb328c0628b1fc17db5c55b8d374e6363466`. Verified the exact published
    commit with the same fetch-and-rebase step used by CPU CI: rebase
    succeeds without conflicts and preserves the tested tree. This avoids
    replaying the conflicting pre-merge barrier-removal commit.
    - On 80.5.9.133 in an isolated development checkout, CPU/mocked
    scheduler, backend, connector, and worker suites: **349 passed, 2
    deselected**.
    - Command: `TORCH_DEVICE_BACKEND_AUTOLOAD=0 python3 -m pytest -q -rs
    --confcutdir=tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store
    tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_pool_scheduler.py
    tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_backend.py
    tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_ascend_store_connector.py
    tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_pool_worker.py -k 'not
    test_joint_prefix_group_ownership_survives_scheduler_conversion_and_empty_pp_layer_names'`.
    - The two excluded existing ownership-conversion cases require
    `vllm.v1.core.kv_cache_planning`, absent from the installed vLLM. Full
    upstream CPU testing remains for CI with aligned dependencies.
    - `bash format.sh ci`: all hooks passed. `git diff --check` against the
    main base passed. The published tree matches the locally tested and
    formatted tree.
    - The MemCache deployment guide and Chinese translations document
    `memcache-hybrid >= 1.3.0` and `memfabric-hybrid >= 1.3.0`; installation
    commands quote these version constraints.
    - Existing backend tests cover retained behavior; barrier-specific tests
    are removed with the feature. No NPU multi-rank startup or end-to-end
    serving validation was run. No production services were modified or
    restarted.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] Boundary / edge-case coverage reviewed; this reverts the removed
    feature and retains existing backend tests.
    - [ ] Regression test added.
    - [ ] Error / failure path execution completed.
    - [x] Meaningful & reliable tests executed.
    - [ ] Performance impact validated on Ascend hardware.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
